WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.699
A little bit later, I'm going to be doing
a deeper, sort of more detailed dove into

00:00:03.699 --> 00:00:07.940
yesterday's very, very unusual press briefing
that Donald Trump gave.

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:13.610
But I want to focus in specifically on something
for a moment where Donald Trump actually said

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:17.200
something that is completely correct, sort
of.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:20.970
But he said it for completely self-centered
and greedy reasons.

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:23.520
And unfortunately, some on the left have kind
of fallen for it.

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:24.980
And it's really disturbing to see.

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:27.250
So let me kind of set this all up for you.

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:34.620
Donald Trump sort of nailed and exposed the
military industrial complex at its core during

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:36.100
yesterday's press briefing.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:38.699
I'm going to play the clip for you.

00:00:38.699 --> 00:00:44.519
The only problem is that he seems to have
no awareness of the fact that he has contributed

00:00:44.519 --> 00:00:52.149
to growing to feeding that same military industrial
complex that he criticized yesterday.

00:00:52.149 --> 00:00:56.550
And, of course, the reason that Donald Trump
said this was to try to make himself look

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:57.550
better.

00:00:57.550 --> 00:00:58.820
That's always Donald Trump's priority.

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:02.539
So let's go in steps as we should.

00:01:02.539 --> 00:01:10.210
Here is Donald Trump explaining why some of
the top people at the Pentagon, as he claims,

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:16.140
do not like him in reference to the story
about Donald Trump allegedly saying troops

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:18.620
who died in combat are losers and suckers.

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:19.940
Here is Donald Trump.

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:25.030
Biden shipped away our jobs, threw open our
borders and sent our youth to fight in these

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:26.590
crazy, endless wars.

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:30.070
And it's one of the reasons the military I'm
not saying the military is in love with me.

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:35.610
The soldiers are the top people in the Pentagon
probably aren't because they want to do nothing

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:40.780
but fight wars so that all of those wonderful
companies that make the bombs and make the

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:44.160
planes and make everything else stay happy.

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:51.910
But so this actually is a critique that makes
a lot of sense.

00:01:51.910 --> 00:01:58.050
Donald Trump points out that part of how the
Pentagon operates and part of how the military

00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:01.250
operates is impossible to extricate.

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:05.630
It's impossible to separate from defense and
military contractors.

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:11.249
I don't remember a Republican president and
even many Democratic presidents so clearly

00:02:11.249 --> 00:02:12.870
calling this out.

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:13.909
Good for Trump.

00:02:13.909 --> 00:02:16.510
He said something that is mostly correct.

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:19.269
Now, there's a couple of problems with this.

00:02:19.269 --> 00:02:25.499
The main problem, of course, is that everything
Donald Trump has done has actually fed the

00:02:25.499 --> 00:02:27.120
military industrial complex.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:28.620
You might think, well, hey, Trump's right.

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:30.910
He didn't get us into any wars as he defines
them.

00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:34.829
He's not the war president, but he's certainly
done some bombing.

00:02:34.829 --> 00:02:36.700
But put the bombing aside for a second.

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:41.430
Donald Trump has bragged his entire presidency
about all of the arms deals and purchases

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:42.609
that he has made.

00:02:42.609 --> 00:02:47.060
He's bragged about how much he sold to Saudi
Arabia and the deal he brokered for American

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:52.439
military contractors to Saudi Arabia the entire
term that he has come up with of refilling

00:02:52.439 --> 00:02:53.650
the cupboards.

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:56.670
He claims the cupboards were left empty by
Barack Obama.

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:59.319
He's talking about military equipment.

00:02:59.319 --> 00:03:05.629
He regularly brags about having rebuilt the
military bigger and better and more powerful

00:03:05.629 --> 00:03:07.019
than ever before.

00:03:07.019 --> 00:03:12.329
That is Trump feeding the military industrial
complex that he sounded like he was criticizing

00:03:12.329 --> 00:03:13.329
there.

00:03:13.329 --> 00:03:18.379
So this was sort of like a rare moment of
clarity for Trump in some sense.

00:03:18.379 --> 00:03:24.010
But it's for completely greedy personal reasons
that he stumbled across something that's sort

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:26.779
of true and he's part of the problem.

00:03:26.779 --> 00:03:31.739
The reason that Donald Trump said this is
not to actually critique the military industrial

00:03:31.739 --> 00:03:32.739
complex.

00:03:32.739 --> 00:03:34.739
In fact, everything he's done has supported
it.

00:03:34.739 --> 00:03:40.590
Trump was trying to explain away why somebody
at the military or the Pentagon might say

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:42.049
something negative about him.

00:03:42.049 --> 00:03:43.599
That is all that he cares about.

00:03:43.599 --> 00:03:47.639
And very sadly, some on the left have fallen
for it.

00:03:47.639 --> 00:03:52.359
I my instinct is that it's the sort of Tulsi
Gabbard crowd.

00:03:52.359 --> 00:03:56.779
They have fallen for this and they are now
saying Trump is well to the left of anybody,

00:03:56.779 --> 00:03:58.709
you know, left of Obama left.

00:03:58.709 --> 00:04:02.980
But no, Trump isn't actually calling out the
military industrial complex.

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:08.290
Trump has bragged for four years about feeding
and fueling the military industrial complex.

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:11.110
And then my my last thought on this.

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:18.340
The military industrial complex isn't even
really generals who want to start wars.

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:23.669
And they're mad at Trump because they won't
let him he won't let them start a war.

00:04:23.669 --> 00:04:28.379
That's not really the way it happens, the
way that the military industrial complex stuff

00:04:28.379 --> 00:04:35.470
happens, the mind the revolving door of money
is lobbyists pushing Congress for pork and

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:41.590
Congress doing it because they want donations
and all of these other projects for their

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:42.680
districts.

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:44.870
That's really the military industrial complex.

00:04:44.870 --> 00:04:48.270
So, yes, Trump is right to some degree.

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:50.590
But the idea that that's how it works.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:56.139
Ignoring the whole lobbying industrial complex
really misses a big piece of it.

00:04:56.139 --> 00:04:57.139
So, okay.

00:04:57.139 --> 00:05:01.870
You know, let let's let's praise Trump to
the degree that he deserves praise.

00:05:01.870 --> 00:05:09.290
But let's understand that he is a huge part
of the problem and is only saying this because

00:05:09.290 --> 00:05:14.349
he's trying to explain away the Atlantic story,
which has, of course, since been corroborated

00:05:14.349 --> 00:05:19.210
by the Associated Press and by Fox News and
by CNN.

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:20.330
We actually do.

00:05:20.330 --> 00:05:24.530
I don't believe that this is being overly
cynical.

00:05:24.530 --> 00:05:26.620
I believe it's being realistically skeptical.

00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:28.240
Tell me if you think I'm wrong.

00:05:28.240 --> 00:06:32.819
Let's now look at some other outrageous moments
from yesterday's press briefing.

